# Values must remain correct through editing

- Make the display format, accepted entry format, canonical payload, and stored value explicit. Use one financial format for the whole affected flow.
- Omar prefers period grouping, for example 10000 displayed as 10.000. For new localized TRY controls, use a decimal comma and Latin digits, for example 10.000,50. Treat this as the proposed Karman financial format, independent of Arabic/English labels, and disclose the choice on first implementation.
- Normalize localized money through an explicit boundary into the existing exact canonical decimal or minor-unit contract. Server-side validation and calculation stay authoritative.
- Existing Purchasing Money::parse interprets a period as a decimal mark. Passing grouped 10.000 directly can become 10.00. Preserve legacy callers and persisted payload interpretation by making localization explicit.
- Use text inputs with inputmode=decimal for grouped money. Consider the installed Alpine Mask $money helper for caret-aware editing and Intl.NumberFormat for presentation after checking availability and behavior.
- A formatter is not a parser or validator. Reject malformed or excessive-precision input before a permissive mask can silently alter its meaning. Preserve blank versus zero, limits, null values, and allowed negative signs.
- Support Arabic/Persian digits by normalization where relevant. Preserve a partially typed decimal, insertion in the middle, selection replacement, Backspace, paste, Tab, Enter, and server-driven resets. Keep formatting local while typing.
- Define the accepted separators explicitly. Reject an ambiguous foreign-format paste with a useful example instead of guessing its amount.
- Use strings or integer minor units for money conversion and arithmetic. Prove round-trip behavior at the supported bounds.
- Reuse one input component and formatter across the affected fields, totals, history, and receipt. Adopt them in other screens when those screens are in scope.
- Treat phone numbers, barcodes, IMEIs, SKUs, and references as identifiers. Preserve leading zeroes and exact characters. Isolate their direction within RTL text.
- Keep dates and times consistent with the operational timezone, Europe/Istanbul. Localize display while preserving canonical storage.
- Label units, currency, required status, and errors. Empty data, unknown values, and zero must remain distinguishable.
